{
  "description": "Shared contract for the channel editor field that edits the legacy `other` value while a typed config override (config.api_version, config.library_id, config.plugin) may also be stored. The relay prefers a non-empty override over `other` (middleware/distributor.go). Go's encoding/json decodes the override from every config key that equals the override key case-insensitively (underscores stay significant); keys apply in document order, so the last string value wins. `config_key` (default `override_key`) is the exact spelling the override is stored and saved under; `shadowed` is an optional earlier spelling whose value the later `config_key` overrides. Every frontend must display `displayed`, and saving with `edit` (null = an unrelated save that leaves the field untouched; a string = the new value typed into the field) must send `payload`: the override spellings of the saved config, in order, are `payload.shadowed` (when non-null) and then `config_key` (when `payload.override` is non-null), and no other spelling. The backend must persist `payload` unchanged, and the relay must then use `effective`. `payload.override` null means the override key is absent from config. Consumed by Go and frontend tests; do not reformat case names.",
